  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 20 files needed for the export-tracking schema migration impact analysis, ordered by relevance:\n\n**Schema / model layer**\n1. `zerver/models/realm_audit_logs.py` \u2014 current tracking mechanism (`AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED = 206`, `RealmAuditLog.extra_data` JSON blob holding `export_path`, `deleted_timestamp`, `failed_timestamp`, `started_timestamp`)\n2. `zerver/models/__init__.py` \u2014 model registry (where a new `RealmExport` import/export would need to be added)\n3. `zerver/models/realms.py` \u2014 `EXPORT_PUBLIC` / `EXPORT_FULL_WITH_CONSENT` / `EXPORT_FULL_WITHOUT_CONSENT` constants (the `export_type` enum the new model's field would carry)\n\n**Direct references**\n4. `zerver/actions/realm_export.py` \u2014 `notify_realm_export`, `do_delete_realm_export`\n5. `zerver/views/realm_export.py` \u2014 `export_realm`, `get_realm_exports`, `delete_realm_export`, `get_users_export_consents`\n\n**Indirect references (the \"tentacles\")**\n6. `zerver/lib/export.py` \u2014 core export logic, `get_realm_exports_serialized`, `do_export_realm`\n7. `zerver/worker/deferred_work.py` \u2014 background worker running the actual export job, reads/writes `extra_data` at each stage\n8. `zerver/management/commands/export.py` \u2014 CLI export command\n9. `zerver/lib/upload/__init__.py`, `s3.py`, `local.py`, `base.py` \u2014 `delete_export_tarball` backend implementations\n10. `zerver/lib/import_realm.py` \u2014 references `REALM_EXPORTED` on the import side\n11. `zproject/urls.py` \u2014 routes wiring the views\n\n**Test coverage**\n12. `zerver/tests/test_realm_export.py` \u2014 dedicated export tests (heaviest user of `RealmAuditLog`/`AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED`)\n13. `zerver/tests/test_import_export.py` \u2014 import/export round-trip tests\n14. `zerver/tests/test_events.py` \u2014 event tests (`check_realm_export`)\n15. `zerver/tests/test_management_commands.py` \u2014 CLI command tests\n16. `zerver/lib/event_schema.py` \u2014 `check_realm_export` schema validator used by the event tests\n17. `zerver/openapi/python_examples.py` \u2014 API doc examples exercising the export endpoints\n\nNote: `zerver/migrations/0595_add_realmexport_table_and_backfill.py` does not exist in this repo snapshot \u2014 the codebase is still on the pre-migration `RealmAuditLog.extra_data` JSON-tracking scheme described above, so that's the actual \"old JSON-based tracking\" being replaced.",
